abstract: >-
  Python reduced-order models and data comparing a conventional Flettner rotor with multifunctional rotors (a
  vertical-axis wind turbine that assists their spin or generates electricity, a telescopic extension, or opening
  into a Savonius turbine) on the ro-pax ferry Galicia on the Portsmouth–Bilbao route, at sea and at berth, with
  hourly ERA5 winds for 2015–2024, a double-multiple streamtube model of the turbine validated against wind-tunnel
  and field data, optimal versus rule-based switching between modes and a Monte Carlo analysis of coefficient
  uncertainty.
keywords:
  - Flettner rotor
  - wind-assisted ship propulsion
  - vertical-axis wind turbine
  - Savonius rotor
  - operating strategy
  - fuel savings
  - ERA5
